            <ArticleTitle>Evaluation of common breast problems: guidance for primary care providers.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>49-63</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The evaluation of common breast problems requires an assessment of the patient's risks and symptoms and a thorough physical examination. When indicated, appropriate imaging studies should be done, the patient should be referred to a surgeon or a breast specialist, and operative interventions should be used.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
